## Lore

One of the glamorous, elite military occupations - the hot-shots who take combat robots like the Dragonwing, Black Knight, Dyna-Max and Devastator into battle. Specialists in giant robots, military aircraft and armoured assault vehicles.

The combat pilot''s job is usually to engage the enemy head on and penetrate enemy lines. They also defend strategic positions, safeguard civilian cities and military bases, support ground troops, and run seek and destroy, reconnaissance and rescue missions.

Alignment: Any.

## The machines

Standard issue includes the X-2000 Dyna-Max, which is not stored: it is a robot vehicle stat block this catalog does not hold. The elite training in it is stored, as a Robot Combat Elite row.

Available upon assignment: any of the X-series robots, additional weapons, energy clips, aircraft and assault vehicles, T-40 plain clothes body armour, a medical kit, portable computer and language translator, plus mid to high level access to military bases, hangars and facilities. The pilot usually gets priority for X-series robots, assault vehicles, aircraft, parts and ammunition.

## Pay

Salary is 2800 credits a month, rising to 4300 to 6000 for ninth level and higher, with quarters, food, clothing and access to power armour storage, robot hangars and maintenance areas provided. Out of the field the pilot gets a private apartment on or near a base.

## Cybernetics

A gyro-compass, headjack and ear implant to start. Additional cybernetics may be purchased or awarded for outstanding service.

## GM Notes

Issued alongside the stored equipment, and not given catalog rows because they are choices the book does not resolve: an energy rifle of choice - typically the TX-42, TX-30 or TX-16 pump rifle - and gun holsters.
